{"id":"essen","name":"Essen","qid":"Q2066","country":"Germany","locality":"Düsseldorf Government Region","lat":"51.450833333","lon":"7.013055555","built":"","year":null,"year_text":"","century":"","era":"Date not recorded","period":"","date_basis":"","style":"","heritage":"","type":"college town; Hanseatic city; big city; urban municipality in Germany; Option municipality; urban district of North Rhine-Westphalia","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Essen","text":"Essen (German pronunciation: [ˈɛsn̩] ) is the central and, after Dortmund, second-largest city of the Ruhr, the largest urban area in Germany. Its population of 573,618 makes it the fourth-largest city of North Rhine-Westphalia after Cologne, Düsseldorf and Dortmund, as well as the tenth-largest city of Germany. Essen lies in the larger Rhine-Ruhr metropolitan region, second largest by GDP in the EU, and is part of the cultural area of Rhineland.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Essen","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-1a224bbbd205","w":1200,"h":796,"title":"Aerial view of Essen.jpg","o":"gh-1a224bbbd205.jpg","credit":{"text":"Drdavid41","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_view_of_Essen.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}}],"depictions":[{"id":"battlefield-1942--essen","game":"battlefield-1942","name":"Essen","verified":false,"text":"Essen is a map featured in the Battlefield 1942: Secret Weapons of WWII. It focuses on the extensive Allied bombings of Essen, which targeted its heavy industrial facilities, especially the Krupp steel and munitions factory. The attackers are the British Commandos, while the defending faction is the German Elite Forces.","text_source":"https://battlefield.fandom.com/wiki/Essen","text_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","images":[{"id":"gh-00d2ff95cd62","w":800,"h":600,"o":"gh-00d2ff95cd62.webp","credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Battlefield 1942, © Elec